{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go | sed -n '117,193p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go | sed -n '1415,1450p'; rg -n 'carried|carry' pose-mcp/internal/cli/testdata/adversarial/README.md; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"   117\t\t}\n   118\t\t// Lexical selection cannot see through aliases. Rather than chase every\n   119\t\t// alias form (review rounds 4–7, N9, N13, N16–N18), a carry needs a\n   120\t\t// case-sensitive filesystem and no tracked symlink that links a module\n   121\t\t// (other than the root) or a declared dependency with any other path.\n   122\t\tmeta, err := loadScopeMetadata(root)\n   123\t\tif err != nil {\n   124\t\t\treturn unused(\"changed-scope selection failed: %v\", err)\n   125\t\t}\n   126\t\t// Symlinks inside a submodule hide behind its gitlink (review round 8,\n   127\t\t// N20): scan each checked-out submodule at its recorded commit, and refuse\n   128\t\t// when a module or a dependency lies in one that cannot be scanned.\n   129\t\tif reason, err := submoduleAliases(root, head, modules, meta); err != nil {\n   130\t\t\treturn unused(\"submodules cannot be read: %v\", err)\n   131\t\t} else if reason != \"\" {\n   132\t\t\treturn unused(\"%s\", reason)\n   133\t\t}\n   134\t\tif link, err := aliasingSymlink(root, head, modules, meta); err != nil {\n   135\t\t\treturn unused(\"tracked symlinks cannot be read: %v\", err)\n   136\t\t} else if link != \"\" {\n   137\t\t\treturn unused(\"the tree tracks symlink %s into or out of a module or a declared dependency, so changes cannot be attributed\", link)\n   138\t\t}\n   139\t\tif caseInsensitiveFilesystem(root, os.Stat) {\n   140\t\t\treturn unused(\"the filesystem is case-insensitive, so changes cannot be attributed to modules\")\n   141\t\t}\n   142\t\t// A case-folded directory inside a case-sensitive filesystem is an alias\n   143\t\t// too (review round 8, N22).\n   144\t\tfor _, dir := range carryRelevantDirs(root, modules, meta) {\n   145\t\t\tif casefoldedDirectory(dir, os.ReadDir, os.Stat) {\n   146\t\t\t\treturn unused(\"directory %s folds case, so changes cannot be attributed to modules\", dir)\n   147\t\t\t}\n   148\t\t}\n   149\t\t// Check ids must be unique: two checks sharing an id would share one base\n   150\t\t// result (review round 7, N19).\n   151\t\tif id := duplicateCheckID(matrix, modules); id != \"\" {\n   152\t\t\treturn unused(\"the matrix defines check %s more than once\", id)\n   153\t\t}\n   154\t\tbaseIDs := map[string]bool{}\n   155\t\tfor _, check := range base.Checks {\n   156\t\t\tif baseIDs[check.ID] {\n   157\t\t\t\treturn unused(\"the canonical result records check %s more than once\", check.ID)\n   158\t\t\t}\n   159\t\t\tbaseIDs[check.ID] = true\n   160\t\t}\n   161\t\tif err := posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"merge-base\", \"--is-ancestor\", base.GitHead, head).Run(); err != nil {\n   162\t\t\treturn unused(\"the canonical result's head %s is not an ancestor of HEAD\", base.GitHead)\n   163\t\t}\n   164\t\tselection, err := computeChangedScope(root, base.GitHead, head, modules, carryExclusions(root, base.GitHead, head, resultsPath)...)\n   165\t\tif err != nil {\n   166\t\t\treturn unused(\"changed-scope selection failed: %v\", err)\n   167\t\t}\n   168\t\tplan.base = map[string]checkResult{}\n   169\t\tfor _, check := range base.Checks {\n   170\t\t\tplan.base[check.ID] = check\n   171\t\t}\n   172\t\t// A module whose checks are not all in the base runs (R3).\n   173\t\tfor _, module := range modules {\n   174\t\t\tif _, selected := selection.Selected[module.Rel]; selected {\n   175\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   176\t\t\t}\n   177\t\t\tstack, checks, _ := moduleValidationChecks(module, matrix, \"\", \"\")\n   178\t\t\tfor _, check := range checks {\n   179\t\t\t\tif check.Program == \"\" {\n   180\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   181\t\t\t\t}\n   182\t\t\t\tid := module.Rel + \"/\" + stack + \"/\" + check.Name\n   183\t\t\t\tif prior, ok := plan.base[id]; !ok || prior.Outcome == \"skipped\" || prior.Outcome == \"\" {\n   184\t\t\t\t\tselection.Selected[module.Rel] = \"carry: no prior result for \" + id\n   185\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n   186\t\t\t\t}\n   187\t\t\t}\n   188\t\t}\n   189\t\tplan.selection, plan.baseHead, plan.baseTime = &selection, base.GitHead, base.GeneratedAt\n   190\t\tplan.record.Used, plan.record.BaseHead, plan.record.Changed, plan.record.Selected = true, base.GitHead, len(selection.Changed), selection.Selected\n   191\t\treturn plan\n   192\t}\n   193\t\n  1415\t\t\t}\n  1416\t\t\tstep.Resolve(cliout.StateFromKey(result.Outcome), note)\n  1417\t\t\tif !verbose && (result.Outcome == \"fail\" || result.Outcome == \"error\") {\n  1418\t\t\t\tstep.Detail(tailLines(result.Output, 10), jsonOut)\n  1419\t\t\t}\n  1420\t\t\trun.Checks = append(run.Checks, *result)\n  1421\t\t}\n  1422\t\trun.WallSeconds = time.Since(wallStart).Seconds()\n  1423\t\t// A check that changed a tracked file changed the material it ran over: the\n  1424\t\t// committed tree no longer describes what was validated.\n  1425\t\tendedClean := materialTrackedUnchanged(root)\n  1426\t\t// The run validated its recorded head only if HEAD never moved: a commit\n  1427\t\t// made while checks ran would let them observe code the record does not\n  1428\t\t// name (review round 4, N10).\n  1429\t\tendHead := \"\"\n  1430\t\tif head, err := gitOutputBounded(root, 1024, \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"); err == nil {\n  1431\t\t\tendHead = strings.TrimSpace(string(head))\n  1432\t\t}\n  1433\t\t// Untracked material created while checks ran counts too (review round 8,\n  1434\t\t// N21): only ignored files may differ from the recorded head.\n  1435\t\trun.MaterialClean = startedClean && endedClean && materialWorktreeClean(root) && run.GitHead != \"\" && endHead == run.GitHead\n  1436\t\t// A run that did not validate its recorded head binds no material: its\n  1437\t\t// bindings would let a later tree make a misattributed pass current again\n  1438\t\t// (review round 5, N12).\n  1439\t\tif len(run.MaterialProvenance) > 0 && !run.MaterialClean {\n  1440\t\t\tfor spec := range run.MaterialProvenance {\n  1441\t\t\t\trun.MaterialProvenance[spec] = posemodel.MaterialBindingUnavailable\n  1442\t\t\t}\n  1443\t\t}\n  1444\t\t// A cancelled run never reads as a success, whatever the severity of the\n  1445\t\t// checks it stopped (review round 1, B5).\n  1446\t\tcancelled := false\n  1447\t\tfor _, check := range run.Checks {\n  1448\t\t\tcancelled = cancelled || check.LimitState == \"cancelled\"\n  1449\t\t}\n  1450\t\tfor _, line := range validationTimingNotes(run) {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"The source sweep found three remaining ways to carry a stale pass: a gitlink nested inside a module can hide a symlink, nested-module changes do not select the enclosing module, and case-folding ancestors are not probed. The targeted regressions pass; these cases are not covered by them. The module-wide validator failed because its subprocesses could not create Go work directories. I’ll distinguish that sandbox failure from the sealed validation results."}}
