{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nThe four prior findings are fixed in their reported scenarios. Three high-severity blockers remain:\n\n- **N24:** Gitlinks nested inside modules bypass the symlink scan.\n- **N25:** Nested-module changes can leave enclosing-module checks carried.\n- **N26:** Case-folding ancestors can evade the filesystem alias guard.\n\n`go test ./...`, build, vet, targeted regressions, artifact-check, and repository-wide strict validation passed. The separate module-only validator failed on read-only scratch creation; its checks passed in the full validator. Persisting assessments were skipped because scratch creation was blocked. New findings are based on source traces and in-memory predicate probes, not newly executed fixtures.\n\nApplied the Go backend, security, documentation-style, and delivery-evidence rules. No repository changes or attestation were written.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R5-N16\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:134-137 invokes the tracked-symlink guard, which checks declared dependency intersections. TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink passed in the targeted Go test run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R6-N17\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The tracked-tree scan no longer depends on Lstat succeeding for the missing dependency leaf. TestCarryRefusesASymlinkInsideAModule at validate_carry_test.go:669 passed, covering deletion beneath b/link.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R6-N18\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:139-140 refuses repository-wide case-insensitive filesystems. TestCarryDetectsACaseInsensitiveFilesystem passed. The distinct mixed-directory ancestor case is reported as N26.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R6-N19\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:151-159 rejects duplicate effective matrix IDs and duplicate base IDs. TestCarryRefusesDuplicateCheckIDs at validate_carry_test.go:729 passed.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N24\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 406,\n      \"summary\": \"submoduleAliases scans a gitlink only when a module is at or below it, or a declared dependency intersects it. It misses gitlinks inside a module. With ordinary modules a and b, put a manifest-free gitlink at b/sub containing link -> ../../a, and let b's check require sub/link/input. A full baseline passes while a/input exists. Delete and commit a/input: selection runs a, but carries b. holds(\\\"b/sub\\\") is false, the superproject symlink scan cannot see through the gitlink, and no other guard detects the alias. This violates R2 and D1 and can turn a currently failing check into a carried pass. Scan gitlinks within modules as well, or conservatively refuse unscanned gitlinks; add the nested-gitlink regression.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N25\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\n      \"line\": 161,\n      \"summary\": \"Selecting only the most specific owner leaves enclosing-module inputs unprotected. Discover modules b and b/n and give b a check requiring n/input. That check reads inside b's own directory and is consistent with the documented selfContained declaration. After a passing baseline, delete and commit b/n/input. Only b/n is selected; b has no required dependency edge and its previous pass is carried even though its check now fails. The descendant-module loop does not select ancestors. R6's ownership rule therefore does not establish D1's unchanged-input guarantee. Select enclosing modules when their directory inputs change, or explicitly define and enforce a narrower module-input boundary; cover both --carry and the shared changed-scope selector.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N26\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 459,\n      \"summary\": \"carryRelevantDirs stops at the nearest existing dependency directory and does not inspect path ancestors. On a filesystem with case-folded directory shared but case-sensitive child shared/a, discover modules shared/a and b and declare b dependsOn=[\\\"shared/A/input\\\"]. The dependency resolves to shared/a/input, but the guards probe shared/a, b and shared/A, not the folding parent shared. Changing shared/a/input selects its owner while the case-sensitive lexical dependency comparison misses b, so b can retain a stale pass. The repository-wide .git probe also passes because the root is case-sensitive. Check ancestor lookup semantics or resolve dependency identity consistently before allowing carry. This mixed-directory platform scenario was source-reviewed, not exercised on matching hardware.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the full implementation diff, scope spec, ADR D1-D3, manuals/help/scaffold, delivery-reader migration, prior regressions, and relevant knowledge/rules. Swept gitlinks and nested submodules, inward/outward/missing-leaf symlinks, case aliases and directory probes, manifest-free moduleOverrides, nested ownership, stack/check-ID changes under an unchanged matrix, criticality and dependency widening, administrative exclusions, dirty/untracked material, pinned HEAD, chained carries, cancellation, and atomic concurrent publication. Targeted tests, full go test ./..., build, vet, artifact-check and repository-wide strict validation passed. In-memory probes confirmed the missed nested-gitlink predicate, omitted parent selection and omitted case-folding ancestor. No carry-specific adversarial-corpus row covers these three cases; existing regression tests do not cover them. No edits or attestation were made.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N26\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Engine, matrix, clean-material and origin checks were examined. Explicit selfContained declarations remain an accepted instance responsibility, but the filesystem probes do not prove the alias assumption required by D1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Carry plans are local to a run; carried entries bypass dispatch. Canonical publication retains the governance guard and atomic publication. Cancellation and origin preservation were inspected.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The JSON additions are optional, and the delivery parser explicitly consumes carried origins while retaining legacy fallbacks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected incompatible-flag refusals, canonical-path validation, revision confinement, malformed metadata, duplicate IDs and full-run fallback reasons.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The CLI result producer and delivery reader preserve the intended per-check head/time boundary; the real parser regression passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Fallback reasons, selection explanations, carried counts and original head/time remain visible. Existing bounded output and environment redaction are retained.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined CLI parsing, additive schema fields, old records without engine_version, and legacy delivery-reader behavior. The intended per-check-origin change is explicitly specified by R7.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N24\",\n      \"rationale\": \"N24-N26 establish remaining stale-pass paths despite the green existing suite.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N25\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Module-level reuse addresses repeated full-matrix cost, but most-specific ownership does not prove unchanged inputs for enclosing-module checks, invalidating D1 in that case.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-a9e60b2a\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR records canonical-result reuse, truthful carried origins, eligibility fallback and the explicit selfContained trade-off underlying D1.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N24\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Manuals, help and changed scaffold sections agree on the intended contract, but their promise to include checked-out submodule symlinks exceeds the actual scan coverage.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected --explain, full-run fallback diagnostics, canonical-path remediation and retained failure outcomes. Recognized eligibility failures are actionable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N24\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R2's submodule alias guarantee is incomplete; N25 and N26 also undermine the unchanged-input guarantee supporting R3 and D1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-36697ddae1f09789\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The source changes remain within CLI selection/result production, delivery parsing, tests and operational documentation declared by the spec. The added ADR governs the public evidence contract.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N24\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Revision confinement and output redaction remain intact, but missed filesystem aliases cross the evidence authority boundary and permit stale passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-36697ddae1f09789\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing module-level results and existing selection is narrower than arbitrary per-check input hashing or output caching. A smaller conservative alternative is refusing unsupported gitlinks and overlapping modules. The design adds no speculative cache framework; its reuse condition must be invalidated by the overlap and alias cases in N24-N26.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exited 0 with orphan warnings. It resolved trailer head e7fdb811fc639f2f4c9f1cd5b693f69400c359a5 rather than the sealed subject; that distinction was retained.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d \\\"$TMPDIR/pose-carry-review.XXXXXX\\\"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Scratch creation failed on the read-only filesystem. Avoided persisting assessment output in the sealed checkout; inspected the spec, ADR and structural delta directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d \\\"$TMPDIR/pose-carry-review.XXXXXX\\\"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No writable scratch copy was available, and the review prohibits repository changes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d \\\"$TMPDIR/pose-carry-review.XXXXXX\\\"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment persists files. Scratch creation was blocked; inspected producer/consumer contracts and used sealed integration evidence instead.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:mktemp -d \\\"$TMPDIR/pose-carry-review.XXXXXX\\\"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment persists files and scratch creation was blocked. Reviewed changed implementation paths directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only precondition: defer until POSE records and verifies the review conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose review-check spec:pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only precondition: this review has not been attested, and the user prohibits recording an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Resolved backend-go with security and documentation-style rules; those rules were applied.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Independently ran pose validate --strict: exit 0, 236 checks passed. Also completed go test ./..., go build ./... and go vet ./... successfully.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Component validation is supported by the sealed canonical result and the successful full strict validator, including all 233 pose-mcp checks. The separately attempted pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp exited 1 because subprocesses could not create Go scratch directories on the read-only filesystem; that invocation itself did not pass.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
